Bug 1: System Allows Booking Appointments in the Past					
					
Severity: Medium (Impacts business logic and scheduling accuracy)					
Priority: High (Essential for a functional Salon ERP)					
Steps to Reproduce:					
					
Log in to the Salon ERP dashboard.					
Navigate to the appointment booking section.					
Select today's date.					
"Choose a time that has already passed (e.g., select 6:00 PM when the current system time is 9:00 PM)."					
Click the "Book" button.					
					
Expected Result: The system should block the booking with an error message stating that past times are invalid for new appointments.					
"Actual Result: The system did not block the action, and the appointment was confirmed ."					
					
Note: unable to provide the screenshot as there is some change in the system and also appointment booking time is not reflecting in the system					
					
Bug 2: Bug/Feature Request: Branch filter does not isolate loyalty members on Members page					
					
"Description: When a specific branch is selected from the top branch switcher dropdown (e.g., ""Main Branch""), the Loyalty > Members directory continues to display all customers globally across all branches, instead of filtering the list to show only the members registered to or associated with the active branch."					
					
Steps to Reproduce:					
					
"Select a specific branch from the global top-left branch dropdown (e.g., ""Main Branch"")."					
Navigate to the Loyalty Members module.					
					
Observe the member list.					
					
Severity: Low (Cosmetic / UI Workflow inconsistency)					
					
Priority: Medium (Important if branches are managed by different staff who should not see other branches' customer lists/phone numbers).					
					
"Expected Result: The member directory filters to only display customers belonging to the selected branch, or the global branch selector communicates that it is viewing ""All Branches"" data."					
					
Actual Result: Customers from all branches are visible simultaneously despite a single branch being selected in the global header.					
					
"=DISPIMG(""ID_ECED6AA1464245A3B9CFC4075D8A5C94"",1)"					
					
Bug 3: Password Validation Fails to Enforce Maximum Length (33 Characters)					
					
Severity: Low (Edge case security validation)					
Priority: Low (Minor UI/Validation fix)					
Steps to Reproduce:					
					
Navigate to the password reset or creation screen.					
Enter a password consisting of 33 characters.					
Submit the form.					
					
"Expected Result: The system should reject the input and display a ""Password too long"" error, adhering to Boundary Value Analysis (BVA) limits."					
Actual Result: The 33-character password was accepted .					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
Bug 4: Missing "Delete" Functionality for Appointments					
					
Severity: High (Critical "missing functionality")					
Priority: Medium (Required for data management)					
Steps to Reproduce:					
					
Open an appointment in the Salon ERP that already has an associated invoice and loyalty points.					
Attempt to find an option to Delete the record to fix an entry error.					
					
Expected Result: An "Owner" or "Admin" should have the ability to delete or remove erroneous records to maintain clean data.					
Actual Result: No delete option exists in the UI; only "Reject" or "Cancel" are available .					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
Bug 5: "PDF is still generating" error when clicking Credit Note on refunded invoice					
					
"Severity: Medium (The core accounting functionality (refunding) works, and data integrity is not lost, but a key user workflow—downloading or viewing the official Credit Note PDF—is blocked.)"					
"Priority: High (Credit notes are compliance and customer-facing documents. Users need to issue or print them immediately after a refund is processed, meaning this blocks daily business operations and customer communications.)"					
Steps to Reproduce:					
					
Navigate to the Invoices module.					
					
"Open an invoice that is marked with the ""Refunded"" status (e.g., Invoice INV-2627-00001)."					
					
Click on the action button to view or access the Credit Note.					
					
Expected Result: The platform should load or download the generated Credit Note PDF document for the refunded transaction.					
					
"=DISPIMG(""ID_310424F60DD04F75ABFA9899264DEBBF"",1)"					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
					
Part 2: Smoke Testing Checklist					
This smoke checklist is a "quick health check" to ensure critical features are not broken after a deployment.					
Area	Expected Result	Status (P/F)			
Login	User redirected to the dashboard.	Pass			
Dashboard	"All modules (ERP, Loyalty, Billing) are visible."	Pass			
Document Upload	File appears in the "Document List" without errors.	Pass			
Send for Signing	PDF directly opens or downloads immediately	Pass			
Notification	Notification is triggered/delivered successfully.	Pass			
Logout	Session is destroyed and user is returned to the login screen	Pass			
